bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    wm_content_damage_plan_api_specified_but_never_landed_2026-11-26, 0, "Measured on release/1.0.0 f2f5776b73f, seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b sha256 fb80903917d6d5f5: 0/7. Six examples fail with variable WM_CONTENT_DAMAGE_FULL not found (spec helper _damage_frame, line 29); the seventh fails on Engine2dCompositorBackend.render_web_draw_ir_composition_resources_revision (already tracked by engine2d_compositor_web_damage_revision_api_missing_2026-11-13). None of WM_CONTENT_DAMAGE_NONE/LOCAL/FULL, WmContentFrame.producer_revision, .damage_mode, .damage_resources_accepted or wm_content_frame_damage_plan_valid is defined under src/ on release/1.0.0 or main, nor in the 2026-09-29 transplant tree 88aac2ffe28, nor in any commit reachable from a local ref (git log --all -S on window_scene.spl). The retained-delta design that did land (586daf45bba, base_content_revision / damage_rects / damage_pixels) is a different mechanism. Needs an owner decision: implement the plan API beside the delta path, or retire the two specs."
    wm_content_damage_plan_api_specified_but_never_landed_2026-11-26, 1, "2026-11-27 fix landed Option 1 beside packed-delta path in window_scene.spl, simple_web_window_renderer.spl, compositor_engine2d.spl, and host_compositor_core.spl; removed @tag:in-development from host_external_content_damage_boundary_spec.spl and wm_external_content_damage_overlap_contract_spec.spl. Verified --mode=interpreter: host_external_content_damage_boundary_spec 7/7, wm_external_content_damage_overlap_contract_spec 2/2, engine2d_frame_switch_receipt_spec 5/5, web_8k_retained_surface_payload_contract_spec 2/2, host_content_frame_admission_spec 1/1, simple_web_window_renderer_spec 28/28, external_web_frame_theme_identity_guard_spec 4/4, host_compositor_pending_damage_spec 2/2, engine2d_compositor_revision_generation_spec 2/2."

